# HEYDAY workflow

## Requirements

- Everything the user states is **acceptance criteria**, not nice-to-have
- Mockups/screenshots are the **acceptance test**, not inspiration
- If ambiguous, ask once — do not silently drop scope
- **Read `heyday-project.mdc`** before implementing; do not rely on chat memory or stale README changelogs

## Feedback word

A user message that is exactly `go`, with no other words, pulls open Feedback bullets, implements the clear ones, pushes them to `main`, and marks only the finished bullets complete. A longer message that contains "go" does not start this. Do not run these steps on any other request.

- `GET https://hub.theheydaygroup.com/api/hub-docs?section=feedback` with no login and no token
- Work only items where `completed` is 0 and `body` is not empty
- Each bullet is acceptance criteria. If one is ambiguous or conflicts with another, skip it, leave it open, and say why
- `npm run build` must pass before any commit
- Commit only the files for the bullets that were finished, then `git push origin main`. This request is the ask to commit and push
- After the push succeeds, `PATCH https://hub.theheydaygroup.com/api/hub-docs/:id` with `{ "completed": true }` and no login for each finished bullet
- Do not mark a skipped or failed bullet complete
- End the reply with a 5-sentence summary of the open bullets, then one short explanation per bullet of how it was solved. A skipped bullet gets the reason it was left open instead of a solution

## Agent prompts (when user asks for one)

Copy-paste block:

```
GOAL · REFERENCE · LAYOUT (numbered) · COMPONENTS (path → duty) · DATA (fields + formulas) · INTERACTIONS · DO NOT · ACCEPTANCE [ ] · VERIFY
```

Use **behavior-level bullets**, not vague labels. Example:

```
Weekly quota cards (PlatformQuotasRow.jsx):
- 5 cards: Marketing Status | Instagram | LinkedIn | TikTok | Newsletters
- Fraction count/target, progress bar, footer NEXT: {title or —}
- GOAL MET if count >= target; ATTENTION REQUIRED if count === 0 and weekday >= Wed
- Target: first integer in platform_goals.frequency, else 2
```

End with: `npm run build must pass. No commit unless asked.`

## UI conventions

- Full width main content — no `max-w` caps that leave dead right margin
- Marketing: slim header, hero calendar — `client/src/components/marketing/`
- Checklists editor: multi-line title, nickname, default assignee, timing row
- `DashboardLayout` + `fillViewport` for transaction workspace and full-bleed pages

## Session handoff

One slice per session (single feature/fix). New chats load rules from `.cursor/rules/` — do not assume prior chat memory.

